Index,SS / Module,Feature,Test Case Name,Test Description,Meta Test Description,Speed,Mode,Memory Start Offset,Memory End Offset,Remarks,Test Steps / Procedure,Meta Test Steps / Procedure,Impacted Registers,Meta Impacted Registers,Validation / Acceptance Criteria,Meta Validation / Acceptance Criteria,Code Generation (Required / Not),Meta Headers,Meta Macros,Meta Arrays
"1","GPIO","GPIO Register Reset Defaults and Masked Read/Write Validation","gpio_reg_wr_rd_test","Validate that GPIO_8 to GPIO_27 registers power-on/reset to their documented defaults and that masked write/read-back operations behave as expected (respecting read/write masks and preserving default values on non-writable bits).","The test first verifies default (reset) values for a list of GPIO registers using default_value_array, ignoring bit[0] by masking with 0xFFFFFFFE. It skips any register marked in skip_rst_array or with read_mask_array == 0x00000000. Next, for each of six data patterns (0xFFFFFFFF, 0xAAAAAAAA, 0x55555555, 0xF5F5F5F5, 0xA5A5A5A5, 0xFFFF0000), it writes (data_wr & write_mask_array[i]) to each address in addr_array, skipping entries per skip_array or where write_mask_array == 0. It then reads back data_rd = read_reg(addr) & read_mask_array[i] and computes the expected value exp_val = (data_wr & read_mask_array[i] & write_mask_array[i]) | ((~write_mask_array[i]) & read_mask_array[i] & default_value_array[i]). A mismatch increments wr_fail_cnt; default mismatch increments def_fail_cnt. Final status is finish(1) if either counter > 0 else finish(0). A soft-reset check function is present but disabled (#ifdef 0).","NA","NA","0x00000000","0x00000000","Bit[0] is ignored during reset-value checks to avoid false mismatches due to input behavior. Non-readable or non-writable registers are skipped based on masks and skip arrays. Arrays list 20 GPIO registers (GPIO_8..GPIO_27). Note: CNT is defined as 49 while arrays are sized 20, which risks out-of-bounds access unless adjusted. The test depends on read_reg, write_reg, wait_on, and finish from the common test framework.","1) Initialize the test and counters. 2) For each target GPIO register (GPIO_8 to GPIO_27), if readable and not marked to skip, read the register and confirm its reset value matches the documented default (ignoring bit[0]). 3) For each of the six data patterns, write the masked value to each writable, non-skipped GPIO register. 4) Read back each register with the read mask applied and compare against the expected value that preserves non-writable bits at their defaults. 5) Record any mismatches and determine PASS/FAIL: PASS if no default mismatches and no write/read mismatches; otherwise FAIL.","1) Call chk_rst_val(): for i in [0..CNT-1]: addr = addr_array[i]; if (skip_rst_array[i] == 1) continue; if (read_mask_array[i] == 0x00000000) continue; data_rd = read_reg(addr); data = (data_rd & 0xFFFFFFFE); if (data == default_value_array[i]) PASS else {def_fail_cnt++; log}. 2) Call chk_rd_wr(): define chk_val[6] = {0xFFFFFFFF, 0xAAAAAAAA, 0x55555555, 0xF5F5F5F5, 0xA5A5A5A5, 0xFFFF0000}; For each j in 0..5: data_wr = chk_val[j]; 2a) Write phase: for i in [0..CNT-1]: addr = addr_array[i]; if (skip_array[i] == 1) continue; if (write_mask_array[i] == 0x00000000) continue; write_reg(addr, (data_wr & write_mask_array[i])); 2b) Read/compare phase: for i in [0..CNT-1]: addr = addr_array[i]; if (skip_array[i] == 1) continue; if (write_mask_array[i] == 0x00000000) continue; if (read_mask_array[i] == 0x00000000) continue; data_rd = (read_reg(addr) & read_mask_array[i]); wr_n = (write_mask_array[i] ^ 0xFFFFFFFF); exp_val = ((data_wr & read_mask_array[i] & write_mask_array[i]) | (wr_n & read_mask_array[i] & default_value_array[i])); if (data_rd == exp_val) PASS else {wr_fail_cnt++; log}. 3) End: if (def_fail_cnt > 0 || wr_fail_cnt > 0) finish(1) else finish(0).","GPIO_8, GPIO_9, GPIO_10, GPIO_11, GPIO_12, GPIO_13, GPIO_14, GPIO_15, GPIO_16, GPIO_17, GPIO_18, GPIO_19, GPIO_20, GPIO_21, GPIO_22, GPIO_23, GPIO_24, GPIO_25, GPIO_26, GPIO_27","MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_9, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_10, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_11, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_12, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_13, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_14, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_15, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_16, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_17, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_18, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_19, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_20, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_21, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_22, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_23, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_24, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_25, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_26, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_27; GPIO_GP0_GPIO_<8..27>_DEFAULT_VAL; GPIO_GP0_GPIO_<8..27>_READ_MASK; GPIO_GP0_GPIO_<8..27>_WRITE_MASK","PASS if: (a) For all readable, non-skipped GPIO_8..GPIO_27 registers, the reset value read (ignoring bit[0]) equals the documented default; and (b) For each data pattern and for all readable/writable, non-skipped registers, the read-back value equals the expected value derived from the write/read masks and default values. FAIL otherwise.","Default check: data = (read_reg(addr) & 0xFFFFFFFE) must equal default_value_array[i] for all i where read_mask_array[i] != 0 and skip_rst_array[i] == 0. Write/read check: data_rd = (read_reg(addr) & read_mask_array[i]); exp_val = ((data_wr & read_mask_array[i] & write_mask_array[i]) | ((~write_mask_array[i]) & read_mask_array[i] & default_value_array[i])); data_rd must equal exp_val for all i, all j in chk_val, where write_mask_array[i] != 0, read_mask_array[i] != 0, and skip_array[i] == 0. Final: def_fail_cnt == 0 AND wr_fail_cnt == 0.","NA","#include <stdio.h>, #include <stdlib.h>, #include \"test_common.h\", #include \"test_define.c\", #include <gpio/gpio_def.h>, #include <gpio/gpio_offset.h>","#define CNT 49, #define SOFT_RST_REG_ADDRESS 0x00000000, #define SOFT_RST_REG_DATA 0x00000000","addr_array[20] = {MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8..MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_27}; default_value_array[20] = {GPIO_GP0_GPIO_<8..27>_DEFAULT_VAL}; read_mask_array[20] = {GPIO_GP0_GPIO_<8..27>_READ_MASK}; write_mask_array[20] = {GPIO_GP0_GPIO_<8..27>_WRITE_MASK}; skip_array[20] = {0...0}; skip_rst_array[20] = {0...0}; local chk_val[6] = {0xFFFFFFFF, 0xAAAAAAAA, 0x55555555, 0xF5F5F5F5, 0xA5A5A5A5, 0xFFFF0000}"
"2","GPIO","GPIO Interrupt Negative Edge Trigger Validation","test_gpio_negedge_intr_en","Validate that each GPIO pad (GPIO_8..GPIO_39) generates and clears a negative-edge interrupt when enabled, and that per-pin and group interrupt status/clear behave correctly through the ISR and system registers.","The test enables the appropriate GIC IRQ (87 for GPIO0, 88 for GPIO1) and enables the GPIO interrupt output in system register INTR_EN1 for the selected GPIO block. It configures each GPIO_8+(i*4) register with bits [20,18,16] set (enable/clear as per IP definition) and initializes the pad driver at 0xA0243FFC to 0xFFFFFFFF. For each pin i in 0..31: clear per-pin raw status via MIZAR_GPIO_GPIO_INTR_RAW_STCLR1 (1<<i), enable only that pin in MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_EN1 (1<<i), arm int_pend=1, then drive a falling edge by writing ~wr_val after a high level. It waits (timeout 5000 with wait_on(10)) for int_pend to be cleared in the ISR. Default_IRQHandler clears int_pend, reads the per-pin register to verify expected bits, checks group status in MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1 contains the pin bit, writes per-pin clear (bits [20,16]) and clears raw status, verifies group status is 0, clears the system RAW_STCR1 bit (GPIO0 or GPIO1), and clears the GIC IRQ.","NA","ISR","0xA0243FFC","0xA0243FFC","Relies on external pad control at 0xA0243FFC to generate edges. Assumes either GPIO0 or GPIO1 is targeted via compile-time defines (GPIO0/GPIO1) to select IRQ and sysreg bits. Uses int_pend flag for ISR handshake and timeout protection.","1) Enable the appropriate GIC interrupt and system interrupt output for the target GPIO block. 2) Configure GPIO_8..GPIO_39 for negative-edge operation and clear any stale status. 3) For each pin, clear raw status, enable its interrupt, arm ISR handshake, then drive a falling edge on that pin. 4) Wait for the ISR to service the interrupt; fail on timeout. 5) In ISR, verify per-pin status and group status reflect the event, clear per-pin raw and group status, clear system-level status, and re-arm for the next pin. 6) Pass if all pins trigger and clear correctly with no timeouts or status mismatches.","test_case(): test_err=0; conditionally GIC_EnableIRQ(87/88). write_reg(MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1, LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1_GPIOx_INTR). write_reg(0xA0243FFC, 0xFFFFFFFF). For i=0..31: addr1=MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8 + i*4; write_reg(addr1, (1<<20)|(1<<18)|(1<<16)); wait_on(10). For i=0..31: wr_val=1<<i; write_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GPIO_INTR_RAW_STCLR1, wr_val); write_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_EN1, wr_val); wait_on(10); int_pend=1; write_reg(0xA0243FFC, 0xFFFFFFFF); wait_on(30); write_reg(0xA0243FFC, ~wr_val); timeout=5000; while(int_pend && timeout--) wait_on(10); if(timeout==0) {printf timeout; test_err++;}. finish(test_err). Default_IRQHandler(): local_wr=1<<i; int_pend=0; write_reg(0xA0243FFC, 0xFFFFFFFF); raddr=MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8 + i*4; rdata=read_reg(raddr); if((rdata & 0x1)!=0) test_err++; if((rdata & 0x2)!=0x0){ rdata_grp=read_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1); if((rdata_grp & local_wr)==0) test_err++; raddr2=base+i*4; write_reg(raddr2, (1<<20)|(1<<16)); write_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GPIO_INTR_RAW_STCLR1, local_wr); rdata_grp=read_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1); if(rdata_grp!=0) test_err++; write_reg(MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1, LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1_GPIOx_INTR); GIC_ClearIRQ(87/88);} else {test_err++;}","GPIO_8..GPIO_39, INTR1_INTR_EN1, INTR1_INTR_STS1, gpio_intr_raw_stclr1, INTR_EN1, RAW_STCR1","MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8 (+ i*4 for i=0..31), MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_EN1, MIZAR_GPIO_GPIO_INTR_RAW_STCLR1, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1, MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1, LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1_GPIO0_INTR, LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1_GPIO1_INTR, MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1, LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1_GPIO0_INTR, LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1_GPIO1_INTR","PASS if each GPIO_8..GPIO_39 pin generates a negative-edge interrupt when enabled, the ISR observes and clears both per-pin and group status, system RAW_STCR1 is cleared, and no timeouts occur. FAIL on any timeout, missing status bit, or uncleared status.","Timeout loop must exit before counter reaches 0; Default_IRQHandler must set int_pend=0. Group status read from MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1 must contain the bit (1<<i) upon entry and return 0 after per-pin clear and raw clear. System RAW_STCR1 write/read must indicate cleared status. test_err must remain 0 at finish().","NA","#include <stdio.h>, #include <lss_sysreg.h>, #include \"test_define.c\", #include <test_common.h>, #include <gpio/gpio_def.h>, #include <gpio/gpio_offset.h>","#define CNT 49","addr_array[20] = {MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8..MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_27}; default_value_array[20], read_mask_array[20], write_mask_array[20] present; skip_array[20] = {0...0}"
"3","GPIO","GPIO Interrupt Positive Edge Trigger Validation (All Pads)","test_gpio_pedge_all_pads_en","Enable positive-edge interrupts for all GPIO pads (GPIO_8..GPIO_39), drive a rising edge on each pad, and verify interrupt generation, servicing, and status clear at both per-pin and group/system levels.","The test enables the target GIC interrupt (87/88) and the corresponding system interrupt output in INTR_EN1 for GPIO0/GPIO1. It programs each GPIO_8+(i*4) with 0x00020000 to enable posedge per pin. It sets GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP1..4 to 0x000000FF to configure GPIOs 8-39 as inputs. It enables all group interrupts in MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_EN1 (0xFFFFFFFF). For each pin i: drive low (0) at 0xA0243FFC, arm int_pend=1, then drive high (0xFFFFFFFF) to produce a rising edge. Wait (timeout 2000) for int_pend to clear via ISR. The Default_IRQHandler reads group status (MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1), temporarily masks group enable (write 0), clears per-pin raw status by writing 0x00010000 to each per-pin register, verifies group status is 0, clears system RAW_STCR1 for the active GPIO block, re-enables group interrupts, and clears the GIC IRQ.","NA","ISR","0xA0243FFC","0xA0243FFC","Uses external pad drive at 0xA0243FFC to generate rising edges for each pin. Requires compile-time selection of GPIO0/GPIO1 to target the correct IRQ and system status bits. The test masks group enable during ISR service to avoid nested events, then re-enables for the next iteration.","1) Enable GIC and system-level interrupt output for the target GPIO block. 2) Configure all GPIO_8..GPIO_39 pads for positive-edge detection and set them as inputs. 3) Enable group interrupt output for all pads. 4) For each pad, drive a rising edge and wait for the ISR to signal completion; fail on timeout. 5) In ISR, confirm group status is asserted, clear per-pin raw status, verify group status clears, clear system raw status, and re-enable group interrupts. 6) Pass if all pads trigger correctly and all statuses clear with no errors.","test_case(): Conditionally GIC_EnableIRQ(87/88). write_reg(MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1, LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1_GPIOx_INTR). For i=0..31: write_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8 + i*4, 0x00020000). wait_on(10). write_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP1..4, 0x000000FF). wait_on(10). write_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_EN1, 0xFFFFFFFF). For i=0..31: write_reg(0xA0243FFC, 0x00000000); wait_on(10); int_pend=1; write_reg(0xA0243FFC, 0xFFFFFFFF); timeout=2000; while(int_pend && --timeout>0) wait_on(10); if(timeout==0){printf timeout; test_err++; break;} write_reg(0xA0243FFC, 0x00000000); wait_on(10). finish(test_err). Default_IRQHandler(): wr_val=1<<i; int_pend=0; rdata_grp=read_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1); write_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_EN1, 0x00000000); if((rdata_grp & 0xFFFFFFFF)==0){printf error; test_err++;} For j=0..31: write_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8 + j*4, 0x00010000); wait_on(2); rdata_grp=read_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1); if(rdata_grp!=0){printf error; test_err++;} Clear system RAW_STCR1 bit for GPIO0/GPIO1 and verify cleared; re-enable MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_EN1=0xFFFFFFFF; GIC_ClearIRQ(87/88).","GPIO_8..GPIO_39, GP0_INTR1_INTR_EN1, GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1, GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP1, GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP2, GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP3, GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP4, INTR_EN1, RAW_STCR1","MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8 (+ i*4 for i=0..31), MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_EN1, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1, MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1, LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1_GPIO0_INTR, LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1_GPIO1_INTR, MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1, LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1_GPIO0_INTR, LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1_GPIO1_INTR, MIZAR_GPIO_GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP1, MIZAR_GPIO_GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP2, MIZAR_GPIO_GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP3, MIZAR_GPIO_GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP4","PASS if each GPIO_8..GPIO_39 pad produces a positive-edge interrupt when enabled, the ISR confirms and clears the group and per-pin statuses, system RAW_STCR1 clears, and no timeouts occur. FAIL otherwise.","ISR must set int_pend=0. Group status from MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1 must be nonzero on entry and 0 after raw clear across all pins. System RAW_STCR1 must indicate cleared status after write. No timeout in waiting loop; test_err == 0 at finish().","NA","#include <lss_sysreg.h>, #include <stdio.h>, #include \"test_define.c\", #include <test_common.h>, #include <gpio/gpio_def.h>, #include <gpio/gpio_offset.h>","#define CNT 49","addr_array[20] = {MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8..MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_27}; default_value_array[20], read_mask_array[20], write_mask_array[20] present; skip_array[20] = {0...0}"